3. Classification of AM for Manufacturing Metallic Components
Currently, there is a wide range of available AM technologies, with each process offering particular advantages and drawbacks depending on its service application. These AM processes are categorized into photopolymerization, material jetting, binder jetting, material extrusion, powder bed fusion (PBF), sheet lamination, and directed energy deposition (DED), as shown in Figure 1 [30]. The focus of this review is on metal-based AM technologies and mainly PBF and DED categories, as they are the most applicable to the aerospace industry.
